    {
      "id": "fd3aaf105dfd-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "Find the LCM of 12, 18, 30?",
      "questionHtml": "Find the LCM of 12, 18, 30?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "90",
          "html": "90"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "180",
          "html": "180"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "60",
          "html": "60"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "120",
          "html": "120"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Prime factorization of 12 = 2<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 3</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Prime factorization of 18 = 3<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 2</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Prime factorization of 30 = 2 × 3 × 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Take the highest power of all prime factors: 2<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>, 3<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>, 5 ⇒ LCM = 2<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 3<span style=\"position: relative; line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span> × 5 ⇒ LCM = 2 × 9 × 5 ⇒ LCM = 180</p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fd3aaf105dfd-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Which of the following options can be used to build the maximum number of meaningful English words using the letters: T, R, A, E, S?",
      "questionHtml": "Which of the following options can be used to build the maximum number of meaningful English words using the letters: T, R, A, E, S?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "2-letter words",
          "html": "2-letter words"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "3-letter words",
          "html": "3-letter words"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4-letter words",
          "html": "4-letter words"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "5-letter words",
          "html": "5-letter words"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given Letters: T, R, A, E, S</strong></p>\n\n<p>For 2-letter words: AS, AT</p>\n\n<p>Total meaningful 2-letter words = 2</p>\n\n<p>For 3-letter&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">words:&nbsp;</span> ARE,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>ART,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>ATE,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>EAR, EAT,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>ERA<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">, </span>ETA,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>RAT, RES,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>RET,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SAT,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SEA, SER,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SET,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TAR,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TEA</p>\n\n<p>Total meaningful 3-letter words = 16</p>\n\n<p><strong>For 4-letter words:&nbsp;</strong>ARTS,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>EARS,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>EAST,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>EATS, ERAS,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>RATS,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>REST,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SEAR, SEAT,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>SERA,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>STAR,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TARE, TEAR,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TEAS,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TSAR</p>\n\n<p>Total meaningful 4-letter words = 15</p>\n\n<p><strong>For 5-letter words:&nbsp;</strong>ASTER,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>RATES,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>STARE,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TARES,<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>TEARS</p>\n\n<p>Total meaningful 5-letter words = 5</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, the option that can be used to build the maximum number of meaningful English words is <strong>3-letter words</strong>.</p>\n\n<p class=\"p1\" style=\"margin: 0px; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-stretch: normal;  line-height: normal; \">Hence, the correct answer is &ldquo;<b>Option 2</b>&rdquo;.</p>\n",
