        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "144",
          "html": "144"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>The logic followed here is that all the numbers except one are perfect squares.</p>\n\n<p>121 = 11<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p>169 = 13<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p>144 = 12<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p>The number <strong>189</strong> is not a perfect square as it cannot be expressed as an integer squared.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, the correct answer is <strong>&quot;Option 2&quot;</strong>.</p>\n",
